   <title>Scenario 2: External URLs</title>
   <shortdesc>Consider a Markdown topic that links to an external website.</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>Kubernetes</keyword>
        <keyword>External</keyword>
        <keyword>URLs</keyword>
        <keyword>external</keyword>
        <keyword>Scenario</keyword>
        <keyword>DITA</keyword>
        <indexterm>Kubernetes</indexterm>
        <indexterm>External</indexterm>
        <indexterm>URLs</indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <prodinfo>
        <prodname></prodname>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <refbody><section><p>Consider a Markdown topic that links to an external website.</p>
<table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
            <title>External URLs</title>
            <tgroup cols="2">
               <colspec colname="c1"/>
               <colspec colname="c2"/>
               <thead>
                  <row>
                     <entry> .md input </entry>
                     <entry> DITA output </entry>
                  </row>                  
               </thead>
               <tbody>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock>For Kubernetes documentation, see
  [Kubernetes Documentation](https://kubernetes.io/docs/).</codeblock>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock>&lt;p&gt;
  For Kubernetes documentation, see &lt;xref href=https://kubernetes.io/docs/ scope="external" format="html"&gt; Kubernetes Documentation &lt;/xref&gt;.
  &lt;/p&gt;</codeblock>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </tbody>
            </tgroup>
         </table>
<p>
            <b>Result:</b> The converter identifies the target as an external URL and generates a DITA <codeph>&lt;xref&gt;</codeph> element with the appropriate scope and format attributes.</p></section></refbody>
